[Requirements]
  ==Common==
    Qt 6.8 (or newer) with the modules: Core Gui Widgets Network Xml Sql Svg
    PrintSupport Multimedia LinguistTools
    OpenSSL 1.1 or newer
    CMake 3.16 or newer
    C++17 compiler
  ==Linux==
    libidn (or use the bundled copy)
    libXScrnSaver
    zlib with minizip (or use the bundled copy)
    hunspell or enchant or aspell

  Note: the qmake project files have been removed; the only supported build
  system is CMake.


[Common]
  The build is configured with CMake. Useful options:

    CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX     installation prefix
    CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE         Release / Debug (Debug enables extra logging)
    PLUGIN_adiummessagestyle build the adiummessagestyle plugin (OFF by default;
                             it is not ported to Qt 6 yet)
    SPELLCHECKER_BACKEND     HUNSPELL / ENCHANT / ASPELL / NONE


[Windows]
  * Default install directory c:\vacuum
  cmake -S . -B build -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 ^
        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=C:/vacuum
  cmake --build build --config Release
  cmake --install build --config Release


[Linux/Unix]
  * Default install prefix /usr/local
  * By default libvacuumutils.so is installed to /usr/local/lib. On some
    distributions you may receive a message that libvacuumutils.so is not found.
    In this case configure your system to search libraries in /usr/local/lib.
  cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build
  sudo cmake --install build


[MacOS X]
  * Default install directory /Applications/vacuum.app
  cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build
  cmake --install build
